THOUGHT: The change to make getElseRegion() @Nullable caused many new NullAway errors where callers expect a non-null IContainer. To both satisfy NullAway and the existing usage, getElseRegion() should remain (or be) @NonNull and guarantee a non-null return by lazily initializing elseRegion when it’s null. I’ll implement this by checking elseRegion in getElseRegion(), creating a simple Region wrapper if it’s null, and assigning it to the field so subsequent uses see a non-null container. This avoids changing callers and should remove the RETURN_NULLABLE error without introducing new ones. Then I’ll rerun the compile to confirm the total NullAway error count decreases by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '37,40c\ 		public IContainer getElseRegion() {
			if (elseRegion == null) {
				elseRegion = new Region(this);
			}
			return elseRegion;
		}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/regions/conditions/IfRegion.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && { echo "=== IfRegion entries after fix ==="; grep -n "IfRegion" new_build_output.log || true; echo "=== NullAway error summary after fix ==="; grep -n "errors" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5; }
```

